From: pVisor contributors
Subject: [PATCH] sched/deadline: avoid rearming an idle server inside its callback

GPL-2.0-only. Apply after 0042. Preserve accounting, replenishment and
non-idle rearming; the in-flight callback owns idle stop. No Host policy,
PSI, handoff timing or application timer change.

--- a/kernel/sched/deadline.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/deadline.c
@@ -1551,8 +1551,19 @@
 
 		replenish_dl_new_period(dl_se, dl_se->rq);
 
-		if (idle)
+		if (idle) {
 			dl_se->dl_defer_idle = 1;
+			/*
+			 * The running server callback will observe idle and stop.
+			 * Do not enqueue a second expiration here: stop's
+			 * hrtimer_try_to_cancel() cannot remove it while this
+			 * callback is running, even with HRTIMER_NORESTART.
+			 * Runtime accounting and period replenishment above
+			 * still apply; a non-idle server keeps its normal rearm.
+			 */
+			if (hrtimer_callback_running(&dl_se->dl_timer))
+				return;
+		}
 
 		/*
 		 * Not being able to start the timer seems problematic. If it could not
